Hi Sharad,

Please use constructBins() function in the mosaics package instead of the perl script process_readfiles.pl <http://process_readfiles.pl> mentioned above. For more details, please read the vignette in the recent mosaics packages, e.g.,

http://www.bioconductor.org/packages/2.13/bioc/vignettes/mosaics/inst/doc/mosaics-example.pdf

constructBins() is available since mosaics version 1.2.3 and you can process the aligned read files within the R environment much more conveniently. I have maintained constructBins(), but not process_readfiles.pl <http://process_readfiles.pl> in the website, since then.

constructBins() supports various file formats: eland result, eland extended, eland export, bowtie, sam, bed, and csem bed. From mosaics version 1.5.2, constructBins() also supports paired end (PET) tag aligned read files in eland result and sam file formats.

Thanks,
Dongjun

